"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SecurityGlyphNotes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3544668776" "The Glyph's Recordings"
// DetailString :
"P220346281" "After finding the Glyph of Unrelenting Memory, you were able to isolate the invasion of the lair. On the recording, you see a strange man speaking before the giant stone doors that secure the base moments before they open wide. To his side, in the flickering light, you see a feminine figure, but do not recognize her. Behind him, there stands a large force of Circle of Thorns members, some of whom are performing rituals that seem to be causing interference in the recording. In the corners of the image, you see some shimmering shadows, but are unable to make out if they are an artifact of the recording or something more sinister.<br><br>Jumping ahead in the recording, you see the Huntress' chambers, where she lies sleeping while the raid begins. In the darkness, you can make out her form just moments before it is swarmed by the same shimmering shadows."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Alysonde1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2719874165" "Raiding Alysonde's Lair"
// DetailString :
"P1076720282" "For a day that started off with a powerful heroine named Alysonde psychically latching onto your mind in desperation, things continued to get stranger. First, the Huntress asked you to raid her own lair for clues to her abduction, an event of which she had almost no memory. However, upon arriving you were astonished to discover that her lair was a captured Circle of Thorns ritual chamber. Less surprising, though, were the numerous members of the Circle who were busy purging the purifying essence of the Huntress from the chamber.<br><br>Upon reaching the central chamber where the glyph was stored, you were also confronted by the former master of the chamber, a very angry demon named Deathfrost. In the tough battle that followed, Deathfrost's ability to convert fear into healing proved a challenge, but you prevailed, once again taking possession of the chamber. Ultimately, though, that was easier to deal with than the actual usage of the glyph itself, which required the distant heroine to use your body as a conduit for unlocking its secrets.<br><br>After finding the Glyph of Unrelenting Memory, you were able to isolate the invasion of the lair. On the recording, you see a strange man speaking before the giant stone doors that secure the base moments before they open wide. To his side, in the flickering light, you see a feminine figure, but do not recognize her. Behind him, there stands a large force of Circle of Thorns members, some of whom are performing rituals that seem to be causing interference in the recording. In the corners of the image, you see some shimmering shadows, but are unable to make out if they are an artifact of the recording or something more sinister.<br><br>Jumping ahead in the recording, you see the Huntress' chambers, where she lies sleeping while the raid begins. In the darkness, you can make out her form just moments before it is swarmed by the same shimmering shadows."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TerminalInformation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1933412960" "Confidential Sky Raider Records"
// DetailString :
"P1926704304" "You have uncovered information concerning a secret project codenamed 'Operation: Huntress'. These files detail Desideratus' plans for Alysonde and her weapons, including the fact that he had hired the Coralax to serve as a stealth force for abducting the Huntress. Also found within the files are orders issued to the Sky Raiders for the complete elimination of all Circle members and Coralax involved in the abduction, in order to prevent the two groups from interfering in his master plan in any way."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Alysonde2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P638409579" "Operation: Huntress"
// DetailString :
"P2527718215" "After rescuing Jackson Carter from certain death at the hands of the Sky Raiders, a point which he strenuously denies, he initially felt compelled to blame you for jeopardizing the undercover investigation he had been performing at the Sky Raider facility. It was, however, a momentary misunderstanding, since a simple review of the evidence from the glyph made it clear that it was ultimately Desideratus who had abducted the Huntress. It was in the course of this discussion that you also learned that one of Carter's allies, Arrawyn, was accompanying the villain as he raided the Huntress' lair, meaning that it was likely she who had sabotaged his operation and revealed him to the Sky Raiders.<br><br>Carter then accompanied you through the Sky Raider facility until you both reached the central SkyDB terminal within the facility. Without a moment's hesitation, Carter unlocked it, allowing you unrestricted access to all of the Sky Raider's internal records, including those detailing their involvement with Desideratus. Among the many records relating to his activities,you found files relating to a secret project codenamed Operation: Huntress.  Searching these records, you learned that Desideratus's ultimate goal was to become the Hunter, killing Krystanova and claiming her power as his own. To this end, he enlisted a diverse array of villain organizations, promising each a great deal. Included in this were the Coralax, who, under the leadership of Devilscale, were the shadowy presence who abducted Krystanova as she slept and were now watching over her weapons for Desideratus. However, the records also contained requests from Desideratus to deploy forces to the lair and the caverns, with orders to eliminate all Circle and all Coralax forces, in an effort to ensure that no one would learn of his true goals and prevent him from executing them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SenDoraLore 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1435024265" "Sen'dora, Bow of the Huntress"
// DetailString :
"P166727178" "This ancient bow, crafted of an extinct species of oak and wrapped with the hide of a sabretooth lion, has been the most enduring symbol of the Huntress' power. It requires no arrows, instead creating its own projectiles from the very life energy of the world, projectiles whose accuracy can be perfected by the Huntress by declaring her quarry. Those pierced by its arrows to not suffer a painful, prolonged death, but are instead lulled quickly into a final sleep. The mystical bow has survived for thousands of years, rendered ageless by a magic long since lost to the march of time."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TheAlorLore 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P457977490" "The'alor, Blade of the Huntress"
// DetailString :
"P3686507790" "A shimmering blade, seeming crafted from pure crystal, The'alor is an unshatterable weapon capable of slicing through flesh and bone with little effort, cauterizing the wound as it cuts. Like Sen'dora, The'alor is truly ancient, but remains ever sharp and without damage through the many thousands of years. In addition to its power as a weapon, it also serves as the focus for the Huntress, allowing the wielder to focus energy upon a target, using the very energy of life to empower allies and consume enemies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PistolsLore 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1013915848" "Raven and Eagle, Pistols of the Huntress"
// DetailString :
"P2654450377" "Far younger than either of the true artifacts of the Huntress, Raven and Eagle are modern semi-automatic pistols wielded by Alysonde. However, despite their comparative youth, both Raven and Eagle have been consecrated as true artifacts. Like Sen'dora, they do not require the Huntress to reload ammunition. However, the ammunition in this case has an extra advantage: it is capable of changing its element to that which would do the most damage to the target. Because these are guns, they do not call as much attention to themselves, and are thus the preferred weapons of the Huntress when among the general populace."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LocationInterrogation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1984080880" "Devilscale's Intelligence"
// DetailString :
"P3145476112" "After confronting Devilscale, the leader of the Coralax clan who signed on with Desideratus, she collapsed in front of you, waiting for you to deal the final blow. When that blow did not come, the angry creature lashed out, demanding that you reinforce its belief in the fundamental evil of 'earthwalkers'. When the deathblow still did not come, Devilscale paused and gave you a chance to explain Desideratus' true intentions. Upon viewing evidence of his treachery, Devilscale gave up the location where Desideratus was hiding the Huntress: within the Temple of the Waters."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LocationPileSearch 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3967374324" "A Musty Tablet Computer"
// DetailString :
"P566929954" "After confronting Devilscale, the leader of the Coralax clan who signed on with Desideratus, she collapsed in front of you, waiting for you to deal the final blow. More than happy to oblige the monster, you struck swiftly, killing Devilscale. Unfortunately, this left you without the information you needed to find where Desideratus was hiding. This led you to continue to scour the cave in which Devilscale was watching over the Huntress' weapons. In the course of this search, you found Devilscale's Hoard, which, surprisingly, contained a tablet computer with information highlighting Desideratus' final location: within the Temple of the Waters."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Alysonde3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2730973147" "The Huntress' Location"
// DetailString :
"P3719497194" "Upon leaving the Sky Raider lab, you again contacted Alysonde, who had fallen unconscious due to the trauma she had sustained. Rousing her, you informed her of your discovery that her weapons were being guarded by the Coralax, but that her location was still unknown. Undeterred, she asked you to confront the Coralax and their leader, Devilscale, in the hopes that you could learn her location and recover her weapons before Desideratus could use them in an effort to claim her role as the Huntress for himself.<br><br>Journeying to the Coralax cavern, you quickly found Devilscale and engaged her in battle. This, in turn, ultimately led to the discovery that Alysonde was being held captive in the Temple of the Waters. After learning this information, you searched the Coralax cavern and recovered the three artifacts of the Huntress, preventing them from again falling into Desideratus' hands."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Alysonde4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1464612865" "The True Goals of Desideratus"
// DetailString :
"P1910748634" "Finally, after systematically working your way through the myriad aspects of Desideratus' plot, you uncovered the truth. Upon exiting the Coralax cavern, you contacted Alysonde one last time. By this point, her torment had pushed her to the brink of death. Hurriedly, you informed her that you had learned her location, whereupon she told you that she, too, had divined her location. Unfortunately, this knowledge for her came at the expense of a nightmarish contact with the Leviathan, who explained Desideratus' true intentions. Desideratus had agreed to serve the Leviathan in exchange for just a portion of its power, and with this power, Desideratus would tear the essence of the Hunter from Alysonde's body. He would then merge both entities into a singular power who would terrorize the world.<br><br>At this point, your mission was no longer about one person, but about saving all life on Earth."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - AlysondeStorySouvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1769322432" "A Feather from the Huntress"
// tDetailString :
"P2904841790" "Alysonde, the Huntress, gave you this magnificent feather from her wings as a sign of gratitude for your courage and your kindness in rescuing her from Desideratus. Whenever you gaze upon it, you are reminded of how you both met, through a rescue you refer to as <br><br><color GoldenRod>All Alone in the Night</color><br><br>It all started when the Huntress herself latched on to your mind, establishing a psychic link with you using the last of her strength and energy. From that unexpected beginning, things continued to get stranger. First, the Huntress asked you to raid her own lair for clues to her abduction, an event of which she had almost no memory. However, upon arriving you were astonished to discover that her lair was a captured Circle of Thorns ritual chamber. Less surprising, though, were the numerous members of the Circle who were busy purging the purifying essence of the Huntress from the chamber.<br><br>Upon reaching the central chamber where the glyph was stored, you were also confronted by the former master of the chamber, a very angry demon named Deathfrost. In the tough battle that followed, Deathfrost's ability to convert fear into healing proved a challenge, but you prevailed, once again taking possession of the chamber. Ultimately, though, that was easier to deal with than the actual usage of the glyph itself, which required the distant heroine to use your body as a conduit for unlocking its secrets.<br><br>After finding the Glyph of Unrelenting Memory, you were able to isolate the invasion of the lair. On the recording, you see a strange man speaking before the giant stone doors that secure the base moments before they open wide. To his side, in the flickering light, you see a feminine figure, but do not recognize her. Behind him, there stands a large force of Circle of Thorns members, some of whom are performing rituals that seem to be causing interference in the recording. In the corners of the image, you see some shimmering shadows, but are unable to make out if they are an artifact of the recording or something more sinister.<br><br>Jumping ahead in the recording, you saw the Huntress' chambers, where she lies sleeping while the raid begins. In the darkness, you can make out her form just moments before it is swarmed by the same shimmering shadows. Upon speaking again to the Huntress, she mentioned that your best lead for chasing down Desideratus was Jackson Carter, who was presently infiltrating the Sky Raiders. Unfortunately, when you arrived at the facility in which he worked, you found that he had been captured by the Sky Raiders. After rescuing Jackson Carter from certain death at their hands, a point which he strenuously denies, he initially felt compelled to blame you for jeopardizing the undercover investigation he had been performing at the Sky Raider facility. It was, however, a momentary misunderstanding, since a simple review of the evidence from the glyph made it clear that it was ultimately Desideratus who had abducted the Huntress. It was in the course of this discussion that you also learned that one of Carter's allies, Arrawyn, was accompanying the villain as he raided the Huntress' lair, meaning that it was likely she who had sabotaged his operation and revealed him to the Sky Raiders.<br><br>Carter then accompanied you through the Sky Raider facility until you both reached the central SkyDB terminal within the facility. Without a moment's hesitation, Carter unlocked it, allowing you unrestricted access to all of the Sky Raider's internal records, including those detailing their involvement with Desideratus. Among the many records relating to his activities,you found files relating to a secret project codenamed Operation: Huntress.  Searching these records, you learned that Desideratus's ultimate goal was to become the Hunter, killing Alysonde and claiming her power as his own. To this end, he enlisted a diverse array of villain organizations, promising each a great deal. Included in this were the Coralax, who, under the leadership of Devilscale, were the shadowy presence who abducted Alysonde as she slept and were now watching over her weapons for Desideratus. However, the records also contained requests from Desideratus to deploy forces to the lair and the caverns, with orders to eliminate all Circle and all Coralax forces, in an effort to ensure that no one would learn of his true goals and prevent him from executing them.<br><br>Upon leaving the Sky Raider lab, you again contacted Avaleys, who had fallen unconscious due to the trauma she had sustained. Rousing her, you informed her of your discovery that her weapons were being guarded by the Coralax, but that her location was still unknown. Undeterred, she asked you to confront the Coralax and their leader, Devilscale, in the hopes that you could learn her location and recover her weapons before Desideratus could use them in an effort to claim her role as the Huntress for himself.<br><br>Journeying to the Coralax cavern, you quickly found Devilscale and engaged her in battle. This, in turn, ultimately led to the discovery that Krystanova was being held captive in the Cavern of the Shaper. After learning this information, you searched the Coralax cavern and recovered the three artifacts of the Huntress, preventing them from again falling into Desideratus' hands.<br><br>For one last time, you contacted Avaleys, whose torment had finally pushed her to the brink of death. When you informed her that you had learned her location, she told you that she, too, had divined her location. Unfortunately, this knowledge for her came at the expense of a nightmarish contact with the Shaper, who explained Desideratus' true intentions. Desideratus had agreed to serve the Shaper in exchange for just a portion of its power, and with this power, Desideratus would tear the essence of the Hunter from Avaleys' body. He would then merge both entities into a singular power who would terrorize the world.<br><br>At this point, your mission was no longer about one person, but about all life on Earth. Without delay, you made your way to the Cavern of the Shaper. With the help of Jackson Carter, you found Alysonde, but not before also eliminating the traitorous Arrawyn. Though she wished to help, Alysonde's body and mind were nearly shattered and it was necessary to escort her to safety outside the caverns. After leaving her in the hands of Jackson's men, you made your way to the final confrontation with Desideratus. Interrupting his communion with the Shaper, you stood against the enraged villain and his minions, dispatching them one by one until Desideratus was defeated."

