"P2994701934" "Sen'dora, Bow of the Huntress<br><br>This ancient bow, crafted of an extinct species of oak and wrapped with the hide of a sabretooth lion, has been the most enduring symbol of the Huntress' power. It requires no arrows, instead creating its own projectiles from the very life energy of the world, projectiles whose accuracy can be perfected by the Huntress by declaring her quarry. Those pierced by its arrows to not suffer a painful, prolonged death, but are instead lulled quickly into a final sleep. The mystical bow has survived for thousands of years, rendered ageless by a magic long since lost to the march of time.<br><br>The'alor, Blade of the Huntress<br><br>A shimmering blade, seeming crafted from pure crystal, The'alor is an unshatterable weapon capable of slicing through flesh and bone with little effort, cauterizing the wound as it cuts. Like Sen'dora, The'alor is truly ancient, but remains ever sharp and without damage through the many thousands of years. In addition to its power as a weapon, it also serves as the focus for the Huntress, allowing the wielder to focus energy upon a target, using the very energy of life to empower allies and consume enemies.<br><br>Raven and Eagle, Pistols of the Huntress<br><br>Far younger than either of the true artifacts of the Huntress, Raven and Eagle are modern semi-automatic pistols wielded by Krystanova. However, despite their comparative youth, both Raven and Eagle have been consecrated as true artifacts. Like Sen'dora, they do not require the Huntress to reload ammunition. However, the ammunition in this case has an extra advantage: it is capable of changing its element to that which would do the most damage to the target. Because these are guns, they do not call as much attention to themselves, and are thus the preferred weapons of the Huntress when among the general populace."

